ARTOMETRICS GLOSSARY — PLACEHOLDER STUB
This is not a binary Adobe Illustrator file.
It is a text brief saved as .ai so an agent can find it next to the HTML starter.
Do not expect Illustrator to open it as vectors or layers.

Style: Art Nouveau
Board: /styles/art-nouveau
Companions: art-nouveau-starter.html, art-nouveau-study.ai, art-nouveau-study.psd

Artboards
1. A vertical poster field, 2400 × 3400 px, paper #f6f1e4.
2. One continuous vine, stroke width varying from 1 px to 8 px, color #1f4d3a, with a second curve in dull rose #c46b73.
3. A circular medallion, stroked in gold #a0782c, left empty. Label it "empty on purpose."
4. A thin gold border. No second typeface. One short line of a serif, if any type at all.

Rules
The curve must arrive: into the border, the medallion, or the other curve.
Do not trace Mucha, Horta, Guimard, Tiffany, or Mackintosh.
No photographic texture. The line is the material.
